  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Jamesville was incorporated in 1785 as James Town, renamed Jamestown in 1797, and finally Jamesville on Feb 10 1855.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofjamesvillenc.com/index.php/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town sits on the Roanoke River, which historically powered sawmills and lumber shipping.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofjamesvillenc.com/index.php/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1869, the Jamesville and Washington Railroad and Lumber Company was incorporated, and by 1870 a narrow‑gauge line reached the town’s timber stands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        7,
        10,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofjamesvillenc.com/index.php/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Jamesville is the second oldest town in Martin County, founded before many neighboring communities.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.townofjamesvillenc.com/index.php/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Astoria Mill, built about a mile upriver, became the county’s largest antebellum industry.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
